        <article class="card step-card">
  <div class="step-header">9. Error handling</div>
  <p class="muted">Goal: handle errors cleanly.</p>
  <img
    class="step-image image-placeholder"
    src="/profile/Error.png"
    alt="Fiori error handling screenshot"
    loading="lazy"
  />
  <details class="code-toggle">
    <summary>See explanation</summary>
    <div class="muted"><strong>General principle</strong></div>
    <div class="muted">
      In SAP RAP, error handling is centralized by the framework. Messages are returned to the Fiori
      UI without UI-specific logic.
    </div>
    <div class="muted">Errors typically come from:</div>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>Validations</li>
      <li>Actions</li>
      <li>Determinations (rarely blocking)</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="muted"><strong>RAP message types</strong></div>
    <div class="table">
      <div class="table-row table-header">
        <span>Type</span>
        <span>Effect</span>
        <span>Usage</span>
      </div>
      <div class="table-row">
        <span>Error</span>
        <span>Blocking</span>
        <span>Invalid data, business rule violation</span>
      </div>
      <div class="table-row">
        <span>Warning</span>
        <span>Non-blocking</span>
        <span>Important information</span>
      </div>
      <div class="table-row">
        <span>Information</span>
        <span>Informational</span>
        <span>User feedback</span>
      </div>
      <div class="table-row">
        <span>Success</span>
        <span>Success</span>
        <span>Action confirmation</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="muted"><strong>In practice</strong></div>
    <div class="muted">Error is most used for critical business rules.</div>
    <div class="muted"><strong>Simple example</strong></div>
    <pre class="code-block">APPEND VALUE #(
  %msg = new_message(
    id       = 'ZMSG'
    number   = '001'
    severity = if_abap_behv_message=&gt;severity-error
    v1       = 'Invalid subscription data'
  )
) TO reported.</pre>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>severity-error blocks save</li>
      <li>the message is displayed automatically in the UI</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="muted"><strong>Coffee Subscription examples</strong></div>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>quantity is zero or negative,</li>
      <li>delivery frequency is missing,</li>
      <li>an action (Pause / Unpause / Cancel) is triggered in an invalid state.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="muted">In those cases:</div>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>a blocking message is shown,</li>
      <li>the object remains in draft,</li>
      <li>the user can correct without data loss.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="muted"><strong>Best practices</strong></div>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>use clear, business-oriented messages,</li>
      <li>block only when necessary,</li>
      <li>keep draft active for correction,</li>
      <li>test messages in the UI.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="muted"><strong>Key point</strong></div>
    <div class="muted">
      Good RAP error handling ensures reliable data, smooth UX, and SAP-standard behavior.
    </div>
  </details>
  <div class="step-takeaway"></div>
</article>
